3. Default Build Behavior (No Precompiled `.o` Objects Distributed)
   Precompiled CuTe-DSL AOT object files (`atlas_fi_gdn_*_prefill*.o`) and their
   generated C headers (`atlas_fi_gdn_*_prefill*.h`) are intentionally NOT
   committed to or distributed with this repository in order to preserve full
   AGPL-3.0 Corresponding Source compliance and avoid redistributing proprietary
   `nvidia-cutlass-dsl` runtime objects.

   By default, `crates/spark-model/build.rs` detects that no AOT `.o` objects
   are present, skips compiling `libatlas_fi_gdn.a` (`cfg(not(atlas_fi_gdn))`),
   and automatically builds with the native CUDA GDN prefill fallback for both
   `ATLAS_TARGET_HW=gb10` (`sm_121f`) and `ATLAS_TARGET_HW=rtx6000` (`sm_120a`).

4. Optional Local Source-Built FlashInfer GDN Acceleration
   Operators who want to enable optional FlashInfer CuTe-DSL GDN prefill
   acceleration locally using their own FlashInfer + NVIDIA CuTe-DSL toolchain
   can export the three AOT `.o`/`.h` pairs from source via:

     repro-kit/source-closure/v0.9.13-r8/gdn-aot/rebuild-aot.sh

   `crates/spark-model/build.rs` searches this directory
   (`crates/spark-model/csrc/fi_gdn/`) for the three AOT object files matching
   `atlas_fi_gdn_<arch>_<target_arch>_prefill{,_f16,_f16_nf8}.o` (with `_`
   stripped from `<arch>`, e.g., `sm121f_aarch64`, `sm121a_aarch64`, or
   `sm120a_x86_64`, plus a legacy `atlas_fi_gdn_sm121a_prefill{,_f16,_f16_nf8}.o`
   fallback for `sm_121*` on `aarch64`), alongside the matching generated
   headers (`atlas_fi_gdn_sm121a_prefill{,_f16,_f16_nf8}.h` included by
   `fi_gdn_bridge*.cu`). Once placed here and `spark-model` is rebuilt,
   `build.rs` automatically detects the trio, compiles the bridge/shim, and
   enables `cfg(atlas_fi_gdn)`.
